      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the idea of a car being mischievous is certainly amusing, I can assure you that mechanics deal with mechanical gremlins all the time! These intermittent noises are often the most frustrating because they are the hardest to pin down, much like a very shy, tiny gremlin hiding under the chassis. It's less about the car being willful and more about a component only reaching its failure point under a very specific combination of temperature, load, and speed. Sometimes, a tiny piece of dried-out grease or a slightly warped mounting point will only cause a momentary squeal when the engine torque spikes during acceleration.",
